Eliza earns $10 per hour for the first 40 hours.

For the first 40 hours:
$$
40 \text{ hours} \times \$10 = \$400
$$

She worked 45 hours total, so the overtime hours are:
$$
45 - 40 = 5 \text{ hours}
$$

Overtime rate is 1.2 times her regular rate:
$$
1.2 \times \$10 = \$12 \text{ per hour}
$$

Overtime earnings:
$$
5 \text{ hours} \times \$12 = \$60
$$

Total earnings:
$$
\$400 + \$60 = \$460
$$

#### 460 [end of text]


